# Repo-root .dockerignore. Needed because backend/docker/Dockerfile builds
# with the repo root as context (see the comment at the top of that file) —
# without this, `docker build -f backend/docker/Dockerfile .` ships the
# entire monorepo (both node_modules trees, the worker's .venv, git history)
# to the daemon before the Dockerfile's explicit COPYs even run. The
# Dockerfile only ever COPYs specific backend/ paths, so none of this was
# ever making it into the image — this just makes the build faster.
.git
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.env
**/*.log
frontend
inference-worker
k8s
docs
